{
  "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
  "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Anya A. Bidwell, Esq., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BIDWELL: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Respondents try to over-read Nieves in two ways. They need to win on both attempts. Each is wrong and would lead to results this Court could not have intended."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Your answer is quite interesting and -- and I think informative because, as you say, if the warrant never should have been sought, it's a different kind of but-for."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: I was just going to ask you whether, on that point of looking at other evidence, would it be consistent with the Nieves exception to look at things other than comparators?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Nicole F. Reaves",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first question presented is narrow, asking only what types of evidence can be used to satisfy the Nieves exception."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Ms. Reaves. ORAL ARGUMENT OF NICOLE F. REAVES FOR THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING NEITHER PARTY"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Can I ask you about the other question presented? You have a footnote, Footnote 6, about abuse of process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, if I read it differently, then what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What would you say in response to the questions that Justice Kavanaugh was asking about the situation where there are plenty of arrests under a particular provision, but in the case at hand, the factual circumstances are quite unusual and there is no"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: If I'm"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. REAVES: So that evidence, standing alone, is not going to be enough to demonstrate that there were similarly situated people who engaged in the same sort of activity who were not arrested."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I, of course, agreed with you in Nieves, with what you just said, but we've crossed that bridge. And you've heard a discussion of what kind of evidence would be necessary to counter the causal connection or to -- to -- to change it, to overcome probable cause determination or the warrant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yeah, I think if -- the way I read Nieves, as the narrow exception that the Court said it was, it should be easy to plead the exception because it's talking about cases where people actually engage in the conduct but officers give a ticket or a citation or a warning or they look away."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the plaintiff has two choices, and she could have had two choices here. She could have at least said I'll allege a comparator."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the Fifth Circuit understood this rule to say you have to show a person within this jurisdiction who has engaged in this conduct before and was not arrested."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: It's good I have an enforcer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0004-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's obvious on its face that this is treating Ms. Gonzalez differently."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BIDWELL",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BIDWELL: I have four points to make."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Police Accountability Project",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0004-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They say that there were only 178 cases overall analyzed, and only 17 cases out of those 178"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1025",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a572b0a3e5b0676a66465756a7f3de4b5633ecd988aa264d0ace7d3fe2162359",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a572b0a3e5b0-0004-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 97,
        "start": 97
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
